From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:42:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] power: supply: macsmc: skip an unreadable manufacture
 date quietly

macsmc_battery_get_date() returns -EOPNOTSUPP when the SMC manufacture
date (BMDT) holds no digits. The power supply core skips a property only
for -ENODEV, -ENODATA or -EINVAL. For -EOPNOTSUPP it logs an error and
aborts, so reading the battery uevent file fails.

On a 14-inch M5 Max MacBook Pro the uevent read printed nothing, dmesg
held 44 "driver failed to report 'manufacture_year' property: -95" lines,
and the synthetic uevent failed with -95.

Return -ENODATA so the core treats the date as absent. Add the 1992 year
offset only when the date was read.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 089b082fa3290813235729582b3d854d602a4d21)
[k114s: from aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1615 (open draft); context offset only]
---
 drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c b/drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c
index 5bd714eaf..174ab5138 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ static int macsmc_battery_set_charge_behaviour(struct macsmc_power *power, int v
 static int macsmc_battery_get_date(const char *s, int *out)
 {
 	if (!isdigit(s[0]) || !isdigit(s[1]))
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		return -ENODATA;
 
 	*out = (s[0] - '0') * 10 + s[1] - '0';
 	return 0;
@@ -760,7 +760,8 @@ static int macsmc_battery_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURE_YEAR:
 		ret = macsmc_battery_get_date(&power->mfg_date[0], &val->intval);
 		/* The SMC reports the manufacture year as an offset from 1992. */
-		val->intval += 1992;
+		if (!ret)
+			val->intval += 1992;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURE_MONTH:
 		ret = macsmc_battery_get_date(&power->mfg_date[2], &val->intval);
